# ==============================================================================
# .dockerignore — what never enters the Docker build context.
#
# This file is not an optimisation, it is a requirement. `docker build` uploads
# the entire context to the daemon before reading the first line of the
# Dockerfile, and this repository keeps a Python virtualenv next to the frontend:
# .venv alone is ~2.5 GB across tens of thousands of files (torch), and
# node_modules is another large tree. Without the exclusions below, every build
# spends minutes shipping files that are then thrown away, and on Render that
# time is billed and counted against the build timeout.
#
# The Dockerfile deliberately uses `COPY . .` for the frontend rather than an
# explicit list of directories. The previous explicit list had gone stale --
# hooks/, pages/, utils/ and public/ were all imported by the app and none were
# copied, so the build failed on a missing module. A denylist here cannot rot the
# same way: a new source directory is included automatically.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Dependencies, both rebuilt inside the image --------------------------
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# --- Build output --------------------------------------------------------
# dist/ is rebuilt by the frontend stage. Copying the host's build in would
# silently ship whatever was last built on Windows.
dist/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# --- Version control and tooling -----------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Caches --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- SECRETS -------------------------------------------------------------
# .env must never enter an image. It holds live API keys and the auctioneer
# password, and anything copied in is recoverable from the image layers by
# anyone who can pull it. Render supplies these as real environment variables,
# which pydantic-settings reads in preference to a file anyway.
#
# .env.example is kept: it is documentation and contains no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Derived state, not image content ------------------------------------
# The player database, the Chroma index and the SCOUT checkpoint are rebuilt by
# POST /api/v1/ingest and live on the Render persistent disk at runtime.
ipl_auction_rag_backend/data/database/
ipl_auction_rag_backend/data/raw/

# --- Not needed at runtime ------------------------------------------------
# The old standalone prototype, superseded by the React console in components/.
auction-console.html
*.md
!README.md

# --- Editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.log
